  "finalText": "The checkmark shows in the off state, which it shouldn't. Its trim has no key before 0.55s, so it sits fully drawn from the start. I'll add a hold at 0 and re-check.\nI built the toggle micro-interaction in the **Toggle** group (track, knob, checkmark) on a light `#f2f2f7` background, and it's checked across the timeline.\n\n- **Off state:** grey track `#c7c7cc`, knob on the left, no checkmark.\n- **0.4s:** the knob starts sliding and the track starts fading from grey to green `#34c759`.\n- **Knob motion:** a Back Out slide with a small overshoot past the end, a horizontal stretch (116%) mid-travel and a squash on arrival, back to 100% by about 0.74s.\n- **Checkmark:** draws on inside the knob from 0.55s to 0.8s.\n- **Settled:** green track, checkmark drawn, knob at rest by 0.8s, held to the 2s end.\n\nThe comp is 2s, so the end holds for about 0.8s. A first pass showed the checkmark in the off state; I fixed it by holding its draw at 0 until 0.55s.\n\nI can make the squash stronger, speed up the crossfade, or add a reverse (on to off) toggle."
